Description




In line with our values of collaboration and integrity, we are seeking a positive and energetic financial controller to contribute to the success of our organization. Reporting to the Director of Finance, the Financial Controller plays a key role in the organization’s financial management. He or she contributes to the reliability of financial information, the optimization of processes, and the rigorous monitoring of projects.








 Responsibilities/Challenges:





Responsible for day-to-day accounting activities (month-end closing, reconciliations, journal entries);




Validate terms and conditions of revenue contracts; set up revenue contracts and financial projects in the enterprise resource planning (ERP) system; coordinate invoicing; prepare claims for government contracts;




Ensure the preparation of financial statements and management reports;




Participate in budget development and budget monitoring;




Ensure financial monitoring of projects (revenue, costs, margins);




Manage and optimize project-based accounting processes;




Collaborate with internal teams to monitor various funding sources;




Ensure the completion of financial audits and regulatory compliance;




Ensure the application of and compliance with current accounting standards;




Manage commercial insurance;




Establish and maintain strong relationships with financial institutions;




Produce financial analyses to support strategic decision-making;




Implement and improve internal controls;




Support the finance team in all projects;









Qualifications:





 Bachelor’s degree in accounting or a related field;




At least 7 years of experience;




Certified Public Accountant (CPA) designation;




Experience in project-based financial management or in a multi-funding environment (strong asset);




Knowledge of ERP systems such as Netsuite (a significant asset);




Proficiency in Microsoft Office, particularly Excel (pivot tables, VLOOKUP function);




Expertise in process documentation.


Bilingualism required due to Canada-wide responsibilities









Skills:





 Interest in and proficiency with software;




Strong organizational skills and the ability to structure one’s work independently;




Ability to thrive in a complex and ever-changing environment;




Demonstrates leadership and problem-solving skills.








FPInnovations respects equal opportunities in employment.
